# BMW 1-series E87 five-door hatchback, 2004-2011.
#
# The first 1-series: the rear-wheel-drive five-door hatch on the E90
# platform, with the long bonnet, the short front overhang and the
# characteristic roofline. The three-door E81, coupe E82 and convertible E88
# are different bodies and are not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_1_Series_(E87)
#
# Dimensions 4.227 x 1.748 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.660 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show the five-door in side, front and
# rear views; the side view governs.
#
# Colours: grade (c), BMW GB colours current across the E87 years: Alpine
# White, Jet Black, Titanium Silver and Monaco Blue. Weights 20, 18, 17, 15,
# total 70, provisional.
#
# Speed 210 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75: a compact but
# rear-drive cabin. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 2004 intro, retires staggered 2026-2029.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-e87.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-e87.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-1-series-e87/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear quarter glass and bumper corners are too
# angular, and the 130i's M Sport diffuser and twin outlets are not reproduced.
# At 128 px the long bonnet, short front overhang and rear-drive five-door
# proportions read as an E87 1-series.


obj=citycar
name=BMW1SeriesE87(AlpineWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=2004
intro_month=9
retire_year=2029
retire_month=6
speed=210
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=443

